---
/* Keep the component samples built and out of the index so changes can be inspected. */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { Code } from 'astro-expressive-code/components';
import { SEVERITIES } from '../config/site';

const sample = `public sealed record Disaster(string Slug, Severity Severity)
{
    public static Disaster Parse(string raw)
    {
        ArgumentException.ThrowIfNullOrWhiteSpace(raw);
        var parts = raw.Split(':', 2);
        return new Disaster(parts[0], Enum.Parse<Severity>(parts[1], true));
    }
}`;
---

<Base title="Kitchen sink" description="Design system proof page." noindex>
  <main id="main">
    <section class="shell">
      <div class="pagehead">
        <p class="eyebrow">Design system</p>
        <h1>Kitchen <span class="slash">/</span> sink</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          The site's shared components in one place.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rule major"><h2>Severities</h2></div>
      <div class="chips">
        {
          SEVERITIES.map((s) => (
            <span class={`sev sev-${s.id === 'warning' ? 'warn' : s.id}`}>{s.label}</span>
          ))
        }
      </div>

      <div class="rule major"><h2>Squiggle</h2></div>
      <div class="storyhead">
        <h1>
          The migration that <span class="squiggle"><span>dropped the wrong table</span></span>
        </h1>
      </div>

      <div class="rule major"><h2>Buttons</h2></div>
      <p>
        <a class="btn primary" href="#main">Primary action</a>
        <a class="btn" href="#main">Secondary action</a>
      </p>

      <div class="rule major"><h2>Chips</h2></div>
      <div class="chips">
        <a class="chip on" href="#main">csharp <span class="n">64</span></a>
        <a class="chip" href="#main">aspnetcore <span class="n">41</span></a>
        <a class="chip" href="#main">data <span class="n">28</span></a>
      </div>

      <div class="rule major"><h2>Prose and code</h2></div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Body copy sets in Chivo. Inline <code>var(--tok-key)</code>
          should read against the inset surface, and the fenced block below is rendered by
          Expressive Code using the site's palette.
        </p>
        <h2>A second level heading</h2>
        <blockquote>
          A pull quote gives an idea room to breathe.
        </blockquote>
        <Code code={sample} lang="csharp" title="Disaster.cs" />
      </div>
      <div class="rule major"><h2>Callout</h2></div>
      <div class="callout">
        <span class="tag">What I would do now</span>
        <p>Take the backup first. Then take a second one.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="rule major"><h2>Rows</h2></div>
      <div>
        <article class="row">
          <h3><a href="#main">Stop parallelizing everything</a></h3>
          <p class="meta"><span class="k">Article</span> 12 min</p>
          <p>Parallel.ForEach is not free, and the bill arrives as thread pool starvation.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="row">
          <h3><a href="#main">Repository pattern versus DbContext</a></h3>
          <p class="meta"><span class="k">Video</span> 18 min</p>
          <p>One of these is already a unit of work. It is not the one you wrapped.</p>
        </article>
      </div>

    </section>
  </main>
</Base>
